lengua's own patch for z3's build.

z3 compiles each of its parts, and its executable, as position-independent code, which its shared
library needs. The WebAssembly z3 is one static module and needs none. wasi-sdk 34 doesn't support
C++ exceptions in shared libraries yet (its CppExceptions.md), and it builds its own libraries
with exceptions as plain code ("lots of builds fail with shared libraries and -fPIC",
cmake/wasi-sdk-sysroot.cmake). In WebAssembly, position-independent code also reads the place of
each of z3's data through a global as it runs, which costs time. So the patch compiles the parts
and the executable as plain code: CMAKE_POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE, which the build sets to OFF,
decides for nothing else in z3.

diff --git a/cmake/z3_add_component.cmake b/cmake/z3_add_component.cmake
index 962b02f..e1d9f06 100644
--- a/cmake/z3_add_component.cmake
+++ b/cmake/z3_add_component.cmake
@@ -208,7 +208,7 @@ macro(z3_add_component component_name)
   endforeach()
   set_target_properties(${component_name} PROPERTIES
     # Position independent code needed in shared libraries
-    POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON
+    POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE OFF
     # Symbol visibility
     CXX_VISIBILITY_PRESET hidden
     VISIBILITY_INLINES_HIDDEN ON)
diff --git a/src/shell/CMakeLists.txt b/src/shell/CMakeLists.txt
index c0e9c85..346a11d 100644
--- a/src/shell/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/src/shell/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -36,7 +36,7 @@ add_executable(shell

 set_target_properties(shell PROPERTIES
     # Position independent code needed in shared libraries
-    POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE ON
+    POSITION_INDEPENDENT_CODE OFF
     # Symbol visibility
     CXX_VISIBILITY_PRESET hidden
     VISIBILITY_INLINES_HIDDEN ON)
